.SBTTL	OMRODT	Rodionov's terminal driver
;
; Included by RMONSJ in the middle of TTOINT (Rodionov's monitor only):
; the output interrupt calls ROPRNT for each character instead of the
; ROM's output entry, and the keyboard interrupt calls ROKEY for a key.
; Taken from his monitor word for word (dis2mac.py): labels are R and the
; address the word has in RT15SJ.SYS.  What is known of it:
;
; - ROPRNT draws the characters itself: two tables of 8-byte glyphs (after
;   ROPRNT and after R47300), found through ADD PC (the monitor is moved
;   at boot) - his character set of pseudographics and signs such as (C),
;   which the ROM's font lacks.  Control characters and the ESC sequences
;   go to the ROM-A's own routines by their addresses (the tables after
;   R51324) - so the monitor runs on ROM-A only.
; - ROKEY takes the keys from the MS 7004's USART (177440/177442) and from
;   the ROM-A's queue; Hold Screen (0126) stops the output, its lamp lit by
;   the keyboard commands 0x13/0x11 through the ROM-A's routine at 177040.
; - R50406 rewrites its own CALL to the ROM's entry 160010 and reads the
;   key of the copy protection from the other side of the disk.
;
	.WORD	0
